gned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2} \\\\ -{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({y}_{1}-2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93995/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93995"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93983/selection/cdc45d5ed8e1d73e51792a58875c44f6cad88a393040ed2acbac8aedd8a43ba0" :answer/id #uuid "90960a40-6850-5afd-8e59-1130a341ede1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93983/selection/881a47626e00dfe73b05de83ba81b7d2d64ecabc27b5e90331f0ae7eaf6700b0" :answer/id #uuid "fa0802e8-13b1-5442-bc40-0336d7a2b0c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93983/selection/d2134a9411abb1b49bdcda3d844fecb05f47954df432de60d0583d68b1d73fcd" :answer/id #uuid "d740e8f9-1fdc-578d-a4a1-