a+b=-4+3=-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94045/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94045"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-94040"] :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}\\,+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1$ and $b=2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=1+2=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-94052/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "c76f44ea-0d8e-5912-856a-9da5dc51a4bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94052/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "343e3db9-ee31-5481-b536-0b105a91acd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94052/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "9537d248-bac8-5bf3-83bc-468fb6fbed8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94052/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "155b3a76-c976-